WEBVTT

01:32.258 --> 01:34.719
Of course there's an outside beyond here.

01:34.803 --> 01:39.224
We don't know what happens
behind the teachers' doors,

01:39.307 --> 01:42.811
or where our food comes from,
or what's inside the vents.

01:43.395 --> 01:46.481
All these gaps
make me think of an "outside."

01:47.649 --> 01:50.402
Why would Mimihime want to go outside?

01:51.903 --> 01:53.988
Do you like Mimihime?

01:54.781 --> 01:55.865
Well, yeah.

01:57.117 --> 01:58.118
I see.

01:59.869 --> 02:01.079
Are you okay?

02:04.207 --> 02:06.626
I'm going back to my room.

02:06.710 --> 02:08.461
-I'll come with you.
-It's okay.

02:08.545 --> 02:11.923
Don't worry. I'll use the auto-drive.

02:12.007 --> 02:14.426
TWO CONFESSIONS

02:30.442 --> 02:31.735
Kuku, that drawing!

02:31.818 --> 02:33.820
Kona gave it to me. Isn't it nice?

02:33.903 --> 02:35.280
Give it here.

02:35.864 --> 02:38.074
Why? He gave it to me.

02:38.158 --> 02:40.535
Kona promised to give it to me.

02:40.618 --> 02:41.953
No fair! You get them all!

02:42.037 --> 02:46.416
I like Kona's drawings, too.
Why can't I get one?

02:47.125 --> 02:49.044
-You're right.
-Huh?

02:49.127 --> 02:51.087
Sorry, Kuku.

03:00.472 --> 03:02.807
Hey! What's that for?

03:03.391 --> 03:05.810
Why did you give it to Kuku?

03:06.519 --> 03:08.313
You promised me.

03:09.230 --> 03:11.107
I'll draw the next one for you.

03:11.608 --> 03:12.817
Really?

03:13.401 --> 03:16.488
I like the things you imagine.

03:17.155 --> 03:20.241
Geez. Tokio is such a crybaby.

03:20.325 --> 03:22.243
Just because Kuku got that drawing.

03:30.585 --> 03:32.420
1 NEW MESSAGE

03:33.129 --> 03:35.256
A message from Mimihime?

03:59.114 --> 04:01.032
So sweaty.

04:11.876 --> 04:14.879
Wake up, Maru. It's the Man-eater, Hiruko!

04:15.797 --> 04:18.341
No good. It's locked.

04:18.425 --> 04:19.759
I'll go out through the bathroom.

04:23.680 --> 04:25.432
Wake up.

04:25.515 --> 04:29.728
She fed us some sort of drug
to put us to sleep.

04:37.235 --> 04:39.487
You two! It's dangerous. Get back inside!

04:39.571 --> 04:42.449
I told you we can kill it.

04:45.827 --> 04:46.828
The Kiru-Beam?

04:47.328 --> 04:48.455
Fully charged.

04:51.666 --> 04:53.335
-There!
-Huh?

05:10.977 --> 05:12.062
Whoa!

05:13.104 --> 05:14.689
I'm okay. Just tripped.

05:26.659 --> 05:28.119
What was that?

05:28.203 --> 05:30.372
Maru, try throwing something.

05:30.455 --> 05:32.040
Okay!

05:32.123 --> 05:34.209
An ultrasonic blast?

05:34.292 --> 05:36.544
No, I see something flickering.

05:37.545 --> 05:39.464
That's not the sound of its voice.

05:41.174 --> 05:43.510
That's the sound of its whip things!

05:55.772 --> 05:58.942
There are three whips on each arm.

05:59.025 --> 06:02.028
I can't get close unless we destroy them.

06:02.112 --> 06:04.489
Three? Gotta get the wings, too.

06:05.115 --> 06:06.616
Are there enough bullets?

06:07.158 --> 06:10.161
No, three and three makes six.

06:10.245 --> 06:11.329
I know that.

06:12.122 --> 06:13.248
Wait…

06:14.082 --> 06:15.500
Where is it?

06:18.461 --> 06:19.713
This way!

06:27.303 --> 06:28.388
Yes!

06:28.471 --> 06:30.640
I hit an arm and a wing!

06:30.724 --> 06:31.891
What a sniper.

06:31.975 --> 06:34.310
The gun's range
is a bit longer than the whips.

06:34.394 --> 06:38.898
If I can get a bit closer,
I can hit the other arm.

06:38.982 --> 06:40.692
Then you can go after it, Maru.

06:40.775 --> 06:43.153
-Okay.
-Here goes.

06:43.236 --> 06:46.364
You'll lose an arm if you get too close.
Be careful.

06:47.574 --> 06:49.826
I was trying not to think about that…

07:16.895 --> 07:17.896
Here!

07:20.482 --> 07:22.067
The manager?

07:22.150 --> 07:23.943
Run! Get away!

07:25.528 --> 07:28.573
Stop! That's my son.

07:29.366 --> 07:31.993
So your son was eaten by that thing.

07:32.077 --> 07:37.207
No. Yuto went inside it,
and it became Yuto!

07:38.416 --> 07:42.962
You drugged us to protect the Man-eater.

07:44.047 --> 07:46.591
I was almost eaten by one, so I know…

07:47.592 --> 07:50.845
It cuts up its prey and absorbs them.

07:51.471 --> 07:54.099
But I'm sorry, I don't think those
who are eaten take over its body.

07:54.182 --> 07:55.975
But that is Yuto!

07:56.559 --> 07:57.852
He protects me.

07:57.936 --> 08:02.399
He even rescued me when I was attacked.

08:05.151 --> 08:06.152
Fine. I get it.

08:07.320 --> 08:08.446
Sis.

08:08.530 --> 08:10.824
I'm out of shots.

08:11.408 --> 08:13.827
If it's not a threat,
there's no reason to kill it.

08:15.620 --> 08:16.746
Yuto!

08:16.830 --> 08:18.832
They understand.

08:19.416 --> 08:21.251
I'm safe.

08:23.378 --> 08:25.839
They can communicate?

08:27.007 --> 08:28.675
See?

08:41.688 --> 08:42.731
Damn it!

08:43.273 --> 08:44.274
Did you see?

08:45.608 --> 08:48.319
The whip only swings in one direction.

08:48.987 --> 08:51.656
So there's a pause between attacks.

08:52.282 --> 08:55.201
How can you think like that?
Someone just died!

08:57.579 --> 09:00.707
If I don't, we won't survive.

09:03.460 --> 09:04.753
Sorry.

09:07.422 --> 09:08.882
I'll kill it.

09:35.742 --> 09:37.160
I got in!

09:58.807 --> 10:02.352
Why didn't Hiruko attack
the manager until yesterday?

10:02.936 --> 10:07.190
Maybe it was her son's consciousness,

10:07.273 --> 10:09.901
or it instinctively kept her alive.

10:10.402 --> 10:13.154
Since its prey gathers around this place…

10:13.655 --> 10:18.535
Maybe she fed the guests to her son…

10:19.953 --> 10:21.121
Let's stop.

10:21.204 --> 10:22.997
The truth can stay hidden.

10:23.581 --> 10:26.251
We already have enough on our hands.

10:26.835 --> 10:29.087
Looking for "Heaven."

10:30.463 --> 10:32.507
Oh, the batteries. Want to take them?

10:33.091 --> 10:35.593
Didn't you give them to the manager?

10:39.973 --> 10:42.142
Hey, stop that!

10:44.561 --> 10:48.064
Sis, have you ever ridden a moving train?

10:48.148 --> 10:50.984
I was three during the Great Disaster.

10:51.067 --> 10:53.403
I wouldn't remember even if I had.

10:53.903 --> 10:54.904
Wait.

10:54.988 --> 10:57.949
If you're 20, then you were five--

10:58.033 --> 10:59.034
Hey!

10:59.117 --> 11:01.161
Is that water safe?

11:01.244 --> 11:03.580
It's okay, I'm just rinsing my mouth.

11:03.663 --> 11:05.373
Plus, it doesn't taste weird.

11:06.416 --> 11:07.876
It's such a nice day.

11:08.460 --> 11:10.295
Perfect for sailing.

11:12.130 --> 11:14.132
KIRUKO-MARU

11:16.176 --> 11:17.177
Okay.

11:17.802 --> 11:18.845
Let's go down.

11:26.936 --> 11:30.065
It's shakier than I thought!

11:30.857 --> 11:32.317
Get on gently!

11:32.400 --> 11:33.902
Step like a feather.

11:33.985 --> 11:35.487
That's impossible!

11:36.571 --> 11:37.739
All right!

11:37.822 --> 11:39.991
It's floating somehow.

11:40.825 --> 11:45.663
If those old guys were telling the truth,
Tomato Heaven is right in front of us.

11:46.623 --> 11:51.670
Kind of late to ask, but there aren't
any sharks or crocodiles, right?

11:54.673 --> 11:56.257
-Don't know.
-Hey!

11:56.341 --> 11:58.927
The only thing I can kill is Hiruko!

11:59.010 --> 12:02.138
You gotta do something if a croc shows up.

12:02.222 --> 12:05.266
I-- I'll think of something
before you get eaten up.

12:05.350 --> 12:07.977
You can't let it bite me.
You're the bodyguard!

12:09.229 --> 12:13.024
If I was a crocodile, I'd eat you first.

12:14.693 --> 12:16.778
Row! Go all out!

12:16.861 --> 12:19.322
It's not that far.

12:19.406 --> 12:22.742
Just keep praying
that a carnivore doesn't show up!

12:25.787 --> 12:26.955
Sorry.

12:27.038 --> 12:29.207
It's okay. I'll go get it.

12:35.630 --> 12:37.507
<i>The teachers-only door.</i>

12:38.842 --> 12:41.428
<i>Is the outside behind it?</i>

12:42.762 --> 12:46.182
The ball went over there…

12:46.266 --> 12:48.351
<i>Go ahead and take it.</i>

12:58.903 --> 13:00.613
There it is.

13:02.824 --> 13:04.242
Okay, stick there.

13:04.826 --> 13:07.537
Are you really going to do it?
It's dangerous!

13:07.620 --> 13:12.542
I'm going to test how strong this is.

13:12.625 --> 13:14.919
They'll get mad if you break it.

13:15.003 --> 13:17.088
I said it'll be fine.

13:17.839 --> 13:21.051
Now, I'll begin the great experiment!

13:25.388 --> 13:27.015
Wow!

13:27.098 --> 13:28.475
Amazing.

13:28.558 --> 13:30.518
It's going so high.

13:31.728 --> 13:33.855
At this rate, it'll go all the way up.

13:34.606 --> 13:36.733
Whoa! Hold--

13:46.618 --> 13:48.453
Ouch.

13:54.584 --> 13:56.711
Why is Shiro the one bleeding?

13:59.839 --> 14:00.882
What's wrong?

14:02.801 --> 14:05.136
I get the feeling
something else is going to fall.

14:08.598 --> 14:11.226
If this is "Heaven,"
then my job ends here.

14:11.309 --> 14:13.728
KUSAKABE FARM TRESPASSERS
WILL BE MERCILESSLY KILLED

14:15.063 --> 14:20.443
But you don't know where "Heaven" is,
or what you'll do when you get there.

14:20.527 --> 14:21.736
Yup.

14:21.820 --> 14:26.366
So my job doesn't end
until you're satisfied with the results.

14:26.908 --> 14:31.663
I'll do everything I can,
so don't keep any secrets from me.

14:32.455 --> 14:34.624
I'm not hiding anything, but…

14:35.834 --> 14:36.876
This.

14:39.295 --> 14:42.132
There's a needle and a drug
inside this cylinder.

14:43.758 --> 14:47.679
There's a guy with the same face as me
out there somewhere.

14:48.847 --> 14:52.183
I was told to inject him with this drug
when I find him.

14:52.892 --> 14:56.771
I believe that the person I'm looking for,
is in this place called "Heaven."

14:57.480 --> 14:58.898
And after the shot?

14:59.399 --> 15:02.193
Don't know. He'll get better?

15:02.861 --> 15:06.364
Anyway, I was told it would help everyone.

15:07.282 --> 15:09.659
I don't know anything else.

15:10.785 --> 15:12.662
Did she tell you anything?

15:13.288 --> 15:16.791
You were the last one to see Mikura.

15:19.461 --> 15:20.545
Pull it down.

15:24.549 --> 15:27.927
Protect Maru with this.

15:28.803 --> 15:31.264
I will. Where should I take him?

15:33.308 --> 15:34.392
Hea…

15:36.311 --> 15:39.814
She only told me to take you to "Heaven."

15:40.357 --> 15:42.108
What're you guys doing?

15:43.401 --> 15:44.778
Hello.

15:44.861 --> 15:47.364
You don't look like bandits.

15:47.447 --> 15:48.740
Are you locals?

15:48.823 --> 15:52.744
No, we walked all the way from Tokyo.

15:52.827 --> 15:54.621
And you found us?

15:54.704 --> 15:57.248
Someone told us about this place.

15:57.332 --> 15:59.334
It's like "Heaven."

15:59.417 --> 16:01.211
So you came here on purpose.

16:01.753 --> 16:03.296
You want to join us?

16:03.380 --> 16:05.465
You see, this kid is--

16:05.548 --> 16:08.593
Let's take them to the Leader.

16:09.177 --> 16:11.346
This way. Come on in.

16:12.847 --> 16:14.057
-Taisuke!
-Yeah!

16:14.891 --> 16:18.853
If you're from Tokyo,
then you climbed down the big fault?

16:18.937 --> 16:21.439
Oh, that huge cliff?

16:22.107 --> 16:25.860
It was so tiring.
We made a raft and crossed over.

16:27.362 --> 16:28.863
That's dangerous!

16:28.947 --> 16:30.782
Saltwater crocs swim in those waters.

16:31.658 --> 16:32.951
What?

16:33.576 --> 16:35.704
There were crocs. Crocs!

16:35.787 --> 16:38.915
You weren't eaten so don't think about it.

16:41.543 --> 16:43.712
I'm Kusakabe, the leader of this village.

16:44.295 --> 16:45.922
This is my wife, Momoko.

16:47.382 --> 16:50.802
As you see, we're just a rag-tag bunch.

16:50.885 --> 16:57.058
<i>We tried to cling to the past,</i>
<i>and dreamt of reviving our society,</i>

16:57.142 --> 16:59.811
<i>but many people grew tired</i>
<i>of such futile hopes.</i>

17:00.520 --> 17:06.568
<i>So we chose a simple life,</i>
<i>living off the fruits of the earth.</i>

17:06.651 --> 17:10.572
<i>It was just my father and a few farmers,</i>

17:10.655 --> 17:12.824
<i>but we soon became this large family.</i>

17:12.907 --> 17:15.869
Wow. That's awesome.

17:16.661 --> 17:20.457
I heard this is "Tomato Heaven,"
is that right?

17:22.000 --> 17:24.419
It used to be full of tomatoes.

17:24.502 --> 17:27.964
Now we can grow all kinds of local crops.

17:33.428 --> 17:35.972
Tomato Heaven is such a nice place.

17:36.598 --> 17:42.187
A farm this size is amazing,
but something feels off.

17:43.146 --> 17:45.273
They are nice enough to feed us, though.

17:46.441 --> 17:48.818
Well, if you think so, Sis.

17:48.902 --> 17:50.779
Make your own opinions.

17:51.988 --> 17:58.286
Since no one's reacting to your face,
I guess that look-alike guy isn't here.

17:58.912 --> 18:01.915
Right, that's one way to find out.

18:01.998 --> 18:05.752
As if, did you not realize that
this entire time?

18:06.461 --> 18:08.213
That face!

18:08.296 --> 18:11.549
You're Kiriko Takehaya!

18:12.217 --> 18:13.510
The electro-kart racer!

18:14.135 --> 18:16.054
No, you got it wrong.

18:16.137 --> 18:21.184
I was a huge fan.
Look, I still have your photo.

18:22.394 --> 18:25.772
How long since you disappeared?

18:26.314 --> 18:28.733
Five years? I was so worried.

18:29.609 --> 18:33.780
There were rumors that you lost it
after killing your brother in a race.

18:33.863 --> 18:34.864
Hey!

18:36.241 --> 18:37.450
She doesn't look--

18:42.497 --> 18:45.333
They might look alike, but that's not her.

18:45.417 --> 18:48.503
-But--
-I said you got the wrong person!

18:49.087 --> 18:50.755
So sorry.

18:51.339 --> 18:52.632
Wait!

18:53.842 --> 18:55.093
I just…

18:57.804 --> 19:00.598
This! Sis, doesn't this look familiar?

19:02.225 --> 19:04.352
Maybe, maybe not…

19:04.436 --> 19:05.770
I got it! It's here!

19:07.397 --> 19:09.774
Don't go around groping someone's leg.

19:09.858 --> 19:12.652
No, this.

19:17.574 --> 19:19.909
Where did you get this box?

19:20.660 --> 19:21.745
Not sure.

19:22.370 --> 19:26.791
We're always taking vegetables
and stuff to Tokyo on the ship.

19:26.875 --> 19:30.628
Boxes like this can come from anywhere.

19:30.712 --> 19:33.298
You can get to Tokyo by ship?

19:33.381 --> 19:34.507
Wow.

19:34.591 --> 19:38.762
If we look into this logo,
won't we find a connection to you, Maru?

19:39.637 --> 19:42.974
At least, we'll find out what it is.

19:43.850 --> 19:48.021
By the way, do you know
of a place called "Heaven"?

19:48.104 --> 19:49.939
-Right here.
-Other than here!

19:54.903 --> 19:58.823
Asakusa during Kiriko Takehaya's era.

20:01.493 --> 20:03.286
Thanks a lot.

20:04.079 --> 20:05.121
That helps.

20:07.040 --> 20:12.128
If we don't get any more information,
let's get on the ship back to Tokyo.

20:12.212 --> 20:13.213
Okay.

20:13.296 --> 20:15.632
Japan is much bigger than I thought.

20:16.299 --> 20:19.761
We'll never find "Heaven" this way.

20:20.929 --> 20:23.056
It's a waste to go back,

20:23.848 --> 20:27.477
but if we investigate your background,
I think we'll get to Heaven faster.

20:30.814 --> 20:34.025
Found some potatoes! Want one?

20:34.109 --> 20:36.194
They won't know if one is missing.

20:37.404 --> 20:40.490
<i>What's wrong?</i>
<i>You don't look good. Seasick?</i>

20:42.283 --> 20:43.827
Forget about Heaven.

20:44.452 --> 20:46.079
We won't find it.

20:46.996 --> 20:50.041
I want to live on the farm with you.

20:50.125 --> 20:52.002
Not me.

20:52.502 --> 20:56.715
Farming all day and getting high at night…

20:56.798 --> 20:59.801
What nature? It's just a bunch of idiots.

20:59.884 --> 21:01.511
That's not what I mean.

21:01.594 --> 21:04.723
I could help you with your job.

21:05.724 --> 21:08.810
I-- I like you, Sis!

21:12.355 --> 21:13.940
DO NOT ENTER

21:14.024 --> 21:18.945
Hey! Confessing in such a place
doesn't do either of us any good.

21:19.029 --> 21:20.739
I'm serious!

21:20.822 --> 21:22.282
Give me a serious answer.

21:25.660 --> 21:29.372
Wait, stop! Get off!

21:29.456 --> 21:30.832
Forcing is--

21:32.792 --> 21:34.711
I'm so, so, sorry.

21:35.795 --> 21:37.839
It's okay. Thanks, though.

21:39.132 --> 21:43.428
Hey, I'm going to tell you something.
So listen.

21:45.388 --> 21:50.894
It might be crazy, but I'm being serious,
so I want you to understand.

21:52.354 --> 21:55.482
My body is a woman's,

21:56.524 --> 22:01.237
but in here, my mind is a man's.

22:03.823 --> 22:07.118
So… I'm a man.

22:09.662 --> 22:10.872
What?
